{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/259983-what-does-your-bolthole-look-like","id":259983,"title":"What does your bolthole look like?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-18T13:01:17-07:00","id":259983,"title":"What does your bolthole look like?","content":"I am preparing a demon campaign and I was wondering about boltholes. Take note that I only possess the core book, I do not have the flowers of hell or any supplement. As such, the bolthole description is really vague and I am still trying to draw some parrallels with demonic lore or anything that could give me some inspiration as to what it would actually look like and what are the many uses you can make of it.<br /> <br /> If some of you already played demon and used boltholes, or if you simply had creative ideas as of their use and appearence I would be glad to read them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3888-freddymontana","name":"Freddymontana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T21:58:31-07:00","id":260363,"title":"","content":"Aether powered computer server towers as an off the grid back up for my tech consumed demon along one wall. A filing cabinet to be filled with pacts or rather decoys and pacts hidden. A simply futon if I must rest my head. It is a bare bones place tailored to my demon. If they don't buy arsenal or some such leave it as a bare room they can store stuff and build up to their ideal safe room. At least that is how I have approached it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T22:01:56-07:00","id":260365,"title":"","content":"Small room, dimensions about equal to the family sedan. The door is a drab olive brown. The walls are institutional grey concrete. There's a cot purchased from military surplus, with an overturned milk crate and a deck of cards. One wall is covered with surveillance photos, maps and blue prints. Most of it just for show. The other wall is covered in weapons, from a pair a trench knives all the way up to an AT4, most assuredly <i>not</i> for show.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}